[E0436] Error: `rest` is used after `grid`, which it refers to, was changed
    ╭─[ err/336_slice_pattern_borrows/main.wip:12:20 ]
    │
 10 │         [first, ..rest] => {
    │                   ──┬─
    │                     ╰─── `rest` refers to `grid`
 11 │             grid[0] = 5
    │             ───┬───
    │                ╰───── `grid` assigned here
 12 │             return rest[0]
    │                    ──┬─
    │                      ╰─── used here
    │
    │ Help: use `rest` before `grid` changes, or take what is needed from it before then
    │
    │ Note: a binding of a pattern on a place refers to the place, so the place must not change while the binding is still used
────╯
[E0405] Error: cannot move `a`, which is behind a reference
    ╭─[ err/336_slice_pattern_borrows/main.wip:18:21 ]
    │
 18 │     [a, ..] => take(a)
    │                     ┬
    │                     ╰── a `match` binding, which refers to part of the matched value
    │
    │ Help: to take the value apart, match it with `match move …`
    │
    │ Note: a reference can read a value but cannot take ownership of it
────╯
